<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">battle-summary</ansi>

When your company's fight ends, you get a short summary of it:

  <ansi fg="command">── The fighting is over ──</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">Damage dealt   Company 96 · Enemies 38</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">Most damage    You 23 · Garrick Vane 21 · Ysolde 18</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">Highest hit    Garrick Vane 11 on bandit captain (critical)</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">Kills          Garrick Vane 2 · You 1 · Ysolde 2</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">Enemies        bandit captain slain · bandit slinger fled</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">Company        You 12/14 · Garrick Vane 6/15 · Tamsin Reed fallen</ansi>

The heading tells how it ended: <ansi fg="yellow">The fighting is over</ansi> (you won),
<ansi fg="yellow">The company is beaten</ansi> (every member fell), or <ansi fg="yellow">The fight breaks off</ansi>
(you fled, broke off, or walked away).

- <ansi fg="yellow">Damage dealt</ansi> counts weapon blows and spells.
- <ansi fg="yellow">Healing</ansi> (when there was any) counts healing your company received.
- <ansi fg="yellow">Effects</ansi> (when there were any) counts effects the blows put on anyone.
- An enemy ends <ansi fg="yellow">slain</ansi>, <ansi fg="yellow">fled</ansi>, <ansi fg="yellow">left</ansi> (walked away), <ansi fg="yellow">beaten</ansi> (a
  practice foe), or <ansi fg="yellow">still standing</ansi>.

A fight is one battle: you, and your company if you have one, against one
group. Fighting alone, you get a summary too. Where several groups wait
their turn, each battle gets its own summary.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">set battlesummary</ansi>
  Turn the summary off, or back on. It's on to start with.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
